<title>USA: C-Cube sees 1996 revenue rise.</title>
<headline>C-Cube sees 1996 revenue rise.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEREY, Calif. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>C-Cube Microsystems Inc, with its late-August acquisition of DiviCom, expects its 1996 revenues to hit $300 million -- up from $124.6 million a year-ago, prior to the acquisition, president and chief executive officer Alexandre Balkanski said at an American Electronic Association investment conference.</p>
<p>He noted that the company's revenues have increased by compound annual growth rates of 100 percent.</p>
<p>Research and development expense has tripled over the last six quarters, he said, and should continue to rise following the acquisition.</p>
<p>&quot;I know these are ambitious goals,&quot; he said after a presentation to analysts.  &quot;We have been a very ambitious company.&quot;</p>
